  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>tr_score_live - the child: scores one batch of orders from Kafka through the H2O scoring service.
Run by tr_live_orders, once per batch. Parameters: SERVICE_URL, MODEL_ID, THRESHOLD (0.15),
CREDIT_CARD_DIR.

1. Get records from stream: key, message, topic, partition, offset, timestamp.
2. json-order: JSON input, the 11 order fields from message.
3. fltr-parsed: Filter rows, transaction_id IS NOT NULL; false to sv-rejected and txt-rejected_messages
   (output/rejected_messages.csv, appended).
4. map-features: Mapping, Credit Card's tr_features.ktr.
5. sv-features: Select values, the ids, the eight features, partition and offset.
6. py-score_live: Python Executor, All rows as batch; scored in the service; kafka_partition and kafka_offset
   kept.
7. iu-live_scores: Insert / Update, fraud.live_scores keyed on transaction_id.
8. fltr-flagged: Filter rows, flagged = 1, to txt-fraud_alerts (output/fraud_alerts.csv, appended, no header).

Shipped data: 500 orders (transactions 212,001-212,500) scored, 5 flagged, 3 of the 6 frauds among
them; a message that is not JSON lands in rejected_messages.csv.</note>
      <xloc>96</xloc>
      <yloc>32</yloc>
      <width>624</width>
      <heigth>314</heigth>
      <fontname>Segoe UI</fontname>
      <fontsize>10</fontsize>
      <fontbold>N</fontbold>
      <fontitalic>N</fontitalic>
      <fontcolorred>0</fontcolorred>
      <fontcolorgreen>0</fontcolorgreen>
      <fontcolorblue>0</fontcolorblue>
